{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"Destinations","modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"Destinations","roleHeading":"Framework"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where tracked events go: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination"},{"text":" is a plain sink with one requirement, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"text":", which is given","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a batch of records, oldest first. Delivering is a chain of operators over a tracker’s records:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"text":" gathers them into batches of 20, and every 30 seconds while any are pending, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"text":" hands each batch to every destination as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lazy unit of work that runs once you call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"execute()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slow one delays only itself. A full buffer drops its oldest batch and reports it as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". When the tracker has a store, the delivery reads the dropped batch’s records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"back for that destination once it catches up, and tells the store when each batch has reached"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every destination."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent categories it serves, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" prints each event, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" keeps the newest records it receives for the app to read, in a debug view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a test.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Logs, traces and servers have destinations in modules of their own, so an app links only the ones","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it uses: ","type":"text"},{"code":"LoggerDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"LoggingDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SpanEventDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TracingDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct Uploader: Destination {","    func receive(_ batch: [EventRecord]) async {","        \/\/ Send the batch, and return once it is somewhere it won't be lost.","    }","}","","let inspector = InMemoryDestination(capacity: 500)","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(","        to: Uploader().accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite(),","        inspector","    )","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let received = inspector.events(of: SignedUp.self)  \/\/ [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The umbrella guide on this area is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Destinations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidCapacity"],"anchor":"Destinations"},{"title":"Delivering","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/batch(clock:)","